  "job_B3.3.18.2_20251003_114703": {
    "text": "Natiuitas Sancte Marie.\nMen \u00f0a leofeste.\nWur\u00f0ie we nu on andweardnysse \u00fea gebyrdtide \u00fe\u00e6re eadige femne sce marie.\n\u00d0eo w\u00e6s godes kenninge ures drihtnes h\u00e6lendes cristes, & hir\u00e6 nome ireht l\u00e6fdi o\u00f0\u00f0e cwen o\u00f0\u00f0e\nHeo is l\u00e6fdi inemned, for\u00f0an \u00fee heo cende \u00feone laford heofen\u00e6s & eor\u00f0\u00e6n.\nAnd heo is cwen inemned, for\u00f0an \u00fee heo com of \u00feam \u00e6\u00f0ele cynne & of \u00feam kynelyce s\u00e6de dauides\nS\u00e6steorr\u00e6 sche is icweden, for\u00fean \u00f0e \u00feeo s\u00e6steorra on niht cu\u00f0e\u00fe scipli\u00f0endum monnum, hwider bi\u00f0\nSwa \u00feenne wear\u00f0 \u00feurh \u00fea halig femne icyd \u00fee riht\u00e6 si\u00f0f\u00e6t to \u00feam \u00e6ce life \u00feam \u00f0e \u00e6r longe seten on\nAnd ha sy\u00f0\u00f0an wisten alle halige \u00feone frumen midd\u00e6neardes & ende & heofene riches wuldor & helle\n\u00deeonn magen we nu hwylcen seogum wordum s\u00e6cg\u00e6n be \u00f0are burdtide \u00fe\u00e6re eadig\u00e6n femne sce marie,\nWe leorni\u00e6\u00f0, \u00fe\u00e6t were sum \u00e6\u00feel wer in israel.\nHis nome w\u00e6s ioachim, of iudan cynne.\nHe w\u00e6s heord\u00e6 his sceap\u00e6.\nHe w\u00e6s godfyrht mon on bilewitnysse & in fremsumnesse.\nAnd n\u00e6fde he n\u00e6nigne o\u00f0re gem\u00e6nenym\u00f0e his eowde.\nOf \u00feam eowde he fedde alle \u00fea \u00f0e heom drihten ondred\u00e6\u00fe & of \u00feam w\u00e6stme he gode \u00fereofealdne lac\nEnne del he sealde \u00feearf\u00e6n & widew\u00e6n & steopcildum & \u00e6l\u00feeodig monnum and o\u00f0erne del \u00fe\u00e6m \u00fee\n\u00deriddan d\u00e6l he heold him seolfum & his hirede bi to lyfigenne.\nFor\u00fean \u00f0e he \u00feas \u00f0ing w\u00e6s donde \u00feus, \u00fea myclode god his woruld\u00e6ht\u00e6; on \u00fea tid n\u00e6s nan mon him\n\u00d0as \u00f0ing he ongon don, \u00fea he w\u00e6s XV wintre.\n& mid\u00fea \u00f0e he h\u00e6fde XX wintr\u00e6, \u00fea nom he wif him to make.\nHeo w\u00e6s ihaten anna.\nHeo w\u00e6s achares dohter of his agene cynne, \u00fe\u00e6t is \u00f0enne of \u00f0am \u00e6\u00feelan cynne dauides \u00fe\u00e6s kynniges.\nHeo \u00fea w\u00e6ron samod togedere twentig wintr\u00e6, swa heo nan bearn ne biget\u00e6n.\n\u00dea ilamp hit summe d\u00e6g, \u00fe\u00e6t heo eoden to \u00feam drihtnes temple, & he \u00fea ioachim stod betwyx \u00feam\nHim \u00f0a to neahl\u00e6hte \u00feare bocere sum, his nome w\u00e6s Ruben, & cw\u00e6\u00f0 to him: Nis \u00f0e ilyfed, \u00fe\u00e6t \u00f0u\nHe \u00f0a \u00fe\u00e6r w\u00e6s mycle scame \u00ferowiende beforan \u00feam folce for \u00f0isse wordum.\nHe \u00fea swa scamiende ut of \u00f0am temple wepende eode & he \u00fea nolde \u00e6ft hweorfan to his agene hame,\n\u00d0a ongon anna hire im\u00e6ccan bewepen & hire to drihtine biddan & \u00feus cw\u00e6\u00f0: Min drihten israele god,\n& ic nat, hw\u00e6der his lif is ofer eor\u00f0an; & gif he for\u00f0iwiten is, \u00feonne gearwode ic him byrigenne.\n\u00d0a heo \u00f0as word icw\u00e6den h\u00e6fde, \u00fea eode heo eft on hire cauertun & hire eadmodlice to drihten bead.\nAnd \u00e6fter\u00fean \u00f0e heo h\u00e6fde hire bone ifylled, \u00fea ahof heo hire eagan up to drihtne.\n& \u00fea iseah heo an sparew\u00e6n nest on anum lawertrewe.\nHeo \u00fea mid wependre stefne clypode to drihtne & cw\u00e6\u00f0: Drihten, \u00feu almihtiga god, \u00f0u \u00fee sealdest\nHw\u00e6t, \u00feu min drihten const & wast mine heort\u00e6.\nHw\u00e6t, ic \u00fee from frim\u00fee mine sinscipes bih\u00e6t, gif \u00f0u me sealdest sunu o\u00f0\u00f0e dohter, \u00fe\u00e6t ic hire wolde\n\u00d0a heo \u00feas word icw\u00e6don h\u00e6fde, \u00fea \u00e6teowde hire godes engel & cw\u00e6\u00fe: Nylt \u00feu \u00f0e ondredan, anna,\n\u00de\u00e6t of \u00fee acenned bi\u00f0, \u00fe\u00e6t bi\u00f0 on wundr\u00e6 allum monnum o\u00f0 \u00f0et woruld\u00e6 ende.\n\u00dea mid\u00fe\u00e6m \u00f0e he \u00feas word icwedon h\u00e6fde, \u00fea w\u00e6s he fram hire eagan ahofen.\n\u00dea w\u00e6s heo swy\u00f0e forht iworden for \u00fe\u00e6s engl\u00e6s isih\u00f0e.\n& heo \u00fea eode into hire cleof\u00e6 & \u00fe\u00e6r wunede \u00f0one d\u00e6g & \u00fea niht on hire bedum.\n\u00dea w\u00e6s morgen iworden; \u00fea la\u00f0ede heo hire \u00f0inene to hire & to hire cw\u00e6\u00f0: Hw\u00e6t, \u00f0u me isawe on\n\u00dea answarde heo hire un\u00f0w\u00e6rlice & hire to cw\u00e6\u00f0: \u00feeah god \u00feinne w\u00e6r \u00e6t \u00fee nome & \u00fein inno\u00f0\n\u00d0a \u00fee heo an\u00e6 \u00feas word ihyrde, \u00fea ongon heo wep\u00e6n biterlice.\nHw\u00e6t, \u00fea on \u00f0are ylcan nihte him \u00e6teowde sum swi\u00f0e wlitig wer on \u00f0am westene, \u00fe\u00e6r \u00fe\u00e6r he w\u00e6s\n\u00dea cw\u00e6\u00f0 ioachi: Twentig wintr\u00e6 ic wunod mid hire & me god nan bearn of hire ne sealde.\nAc ic swi\u00f0e ge\u00e6swicod eode ut of \u00feam godes temple; for\u00fean ic nylle \u00e6ft ham hweorfan, ac ic wylle\n\u00dea andswarde him \u00fee \u00e6ngel & \u00f0us cw\u00e6\u00f0: Ic eom drihtine engel & nu to d\u00e6g ic me \u00e6teowde \u00feine\n& wite \u00feu nu, \u00fe\u00e6t heo of \u00f0ine s\u00e6de ieacnod is, swa swa \u00feu na hit ne wistest.\n\u00d0a \u00fee \u00f0u ane forl\u00e6te, heo \u00fee cenne\u00f0 dohter & heo bi\u00f0 on godes temple fulfremed, & \u00fee halga gast\nCyr nu to \u00f0ine im\u00e6ccan & \u00feu im\u00e6test hire ieacnode, & \u00feas \u00f0once gode, for\u00fean \u00f0e hire s\u00e6d bi\u00f0\n\u00dea weor\u00f0ede hine ioachim & him to cw\u00e6\u00f0: Gif hit \u00feus iwyr\u00f0an scyle, swa \u00f0u cw\u00e6st, site mid me on\n\u00dea cw\u00e6\u00f0 \u00fee engel to him: Hwi wilt \u00f0u la cw\u00e6\u00f0on, \u00fe\u00e6t \u00f0u beo min \u00f0eow\u00e6, ac \u00feu eart min efen\u00f0eow\u00e6,\n& ic \u00fee secge, \u00feet min m\u00e6te and min drync ne m\u00e6g beon from monnum is\u00e6gen.\nAc swa hw\u00e6t swa \u00f0u me to gife tihtest, bring \u00fe\u00e6t gode to uns\u00e6gednesse.\nHe \u00fea ioachim brohte unwemmed lac & to \u00feam engle cw\u00e6\u00f0: N\u00e6s ic na ge\u00f0rystig, \u00fe\u00e6t ic gode\n\u00dea cw\u00e6\u00f0 \u00fee engel: Na ic \u00fee ne hate gode sacerdlice ons\u00e6gednesse bringan, for\u00fean \u00f0e ic godes will\u00e6n\n\u00dea ferde \u00fee engel samod mid \u00feam stence \u00f0\u00e6re ons\u00e6gednysse into heofenum.\nHe \u00fea ioachim wear\u00f0 to \u00feam afyrht, \u00fe\u00e6t he feol on eor\u00fean & l\u00e6g swylce he dead were fram \u00feare\nHim \u00fea to neal\u00e6hton his heord\u00e6s & heo hine \u00fea iseg\u00e6n liogan & nysten \u00feenne inting\u00e6n on him, ac\n\u00d0a ahof he his heafod up & s\u00e6de heom his sih\u00f0e, \u00fee he iseah.\n\u00d0a wyrdon heo son\u00e6 afyrhte & eac wundredon, o\u00f0 \u00f0et he hit heom all is\u00e6d h\u00e6fde; & heo alle \u00fea hine\nHe \u00fea ioachim \u00f0reodode on his mode, hw\u00e6t he embe \u00fe\u00e6t dyde.\n\u00dea wear\u00f0 he fering\u00e6 on sl\u00e6pe gehwirfed.\nHim \u00fea \u00e6teowde \u00fee ilc\u00e6 engel eft on slepe & him to cw\u00e6\u00f0: Ic eom godes engel & from drihtne ic am\nAc fare nu ham orsorh to \u00f0ine m\u00e6ccan & eower mildheortnysse, \u00fee ge wrohton, & eower nom\u00e6 w\u00e6s\nHe \u00fea ioachim of \u00feam slepe aras & his swefen s\u00e6de his heordum.\nHeo \u00fea alle hine bed\u00e6n & halsedon, \u00fe\u00e6t he ihyrsumode \u00feas engl\u00e6s wordum & r\u00e6cene ham cyrde.\n\u00dea w\u00e6s he \u00e6r igan for his unrotnysse on \u00feam westene swa feor, \u00fe\u00e6t he for \u00f0rittige dagene f\u00e6cc ne\nHeo \u00fea anna w\u00e6s \u00e6t hire bede, \u00fea \u00e6teowde hire drihtnes engel & hire cydde \u00f0one hamsi\u00f0 hire imacen.\n& heo \u00fea mid hire hinene him ongean eode mid mycle gefean; swilce eac hire magas & all israel\u00e6\n\u00d0a c\u00e6nde anna hire dohtor & hire nome nemnode maria, & heo hire \u00fea fedde \u00fereo wintr\u00e6 \u00e6t hire\nIoachim & anna \u00fea l\u00e6ddon \u00fe\u00e6t child mid heom to \u00feare halgan ceastre & \u00fe\u00e6t lac brohten mid heom\n& heo \u00fea sealden \u00fe\u00e6t child on gem\u00e6ne \u00fe\u00e6re femen\u00e6, \u00fee d\u00e6ges & nihtes on godes lofe wunoden.\nHeo up eode mid \u00feam o\u00f0re femnum on \u00fea XV st\u00e6pes on \u00fea temple, swa heo ne on beac ne beseah, ne\nAc heo w\u00e6s on geange & on word\u00e6 & on allum ib\u00e6re ilic wunsumen menn, \u00fee h\u00e6fde \u00ferittig wintr\u00e6,\nHeo anna \u00fea w\u00e6s ifylled mid \u00feam halgan gaste & heo witegode \u00fea biforen \u00feam folce & \u00feus cw\u00e6\u00f0:\n& \u00fea \u00f0eode, \u00fee mid us aris\u00e6n, he wolde eadmedigan, \u00fe\u00e6t heo cyrdon to heor\u00e6 silfr\u00e6 heortum &\nOn \u00feam unbeo\u00f0rum \u00e6cere blisse, \u00f0e \u00fear igef\u00e6n is on israele, swa me min drihten geaf, \u00fe\u00e6t ic mot\nDrihten min acerde heom from me & me geaf ecce blisse.\n\u00d0a heo \u00feas word icw\u00e6don h\u00e6fde, \u00fea cyrdon heo ham mid \u00feam & \u00fe\u00e6t child forl\u00e6ten \u00e6t \u00feam temple\n& heo \u00fea weox & wear\u00f0 fulfremed on godr\u00e6 m\u00e6gene heanyss\u00e6, & heo \u00fea son\u00e6 godum towcr\u00e6ftum\nAnd heo sette hire sylf haligne regol, swa \u00fe\u00e6t heo wolde beon fram \u00feare \u00e6reste tyde \u00fe\u00e6s d\u00e6ges on\n& \u00e6ft fram \u00feare nigo\u00f0an tyde heo \u00feurhwunode standende on hire ibedum, o\u00f0 \u00f0et godes engel hire\n& heo sy\u00f0\u00f0an w\u00e6s betere & swi\u00f0re on godes luf\u00e6n & on gastlicr\u00e6 m\u00e6gen\u00e6 heanyss\u00e6, & heo yldr\u00e6n\nHeo w\u00e6s eadmodre & on godes lufe gl\u00e6dre & on \u00feohte cl\u00e6nre & on \u00feam dauidisce sange wr\u00e6stlicre,\n& heo w\u00e6s \u00f0olemod & stea\u00f0ig on hire ib\u00e6rum & nan mon ne seah hire wra\u00f0, ne t\u00e6lan, ne warigen, ne\nAc hire word weron godes gife fulle & he w\u00e6s on hire heort\u00e6n smeagende \u00feone wisdom on godes\n& \u00f0a femnen, \u00fee mid hire weron, heo tymede, \u00fe\u00e6t heo on heor\u00e6 bedum \u00feurhwynedon & on godes lofe\n& of hire aras \u00e6rest \u00fee wun\u00e6, \u00fe\u00e6t \u00f0e mon, \u00f0e o\u00f0erne grete mid leofe worden, \u00fe\u00e6t he him godcunde\n& d\u00e6ghwamlice heo underfeng mete of \u00feas engl\u00e6s handa & mid \u00fean heo ireordod w\u00e6s, & \u00feone mete,\nAnd swa hwilc mon swa hire untrum isohte, \u00e6ft he eode hal from hire.\n\u00dea ilamp hit, \u00fe\u00e6t abiathar, \u00fee sacerd, brohte mycelne gyfe \u00feam biscope & b\u00e6d hine, \u00feet he sealde\n\u00d0a steorde mari\u00e6 him & cw\u00e6\u00f0 andredlice: Ne wur\u00f0\u00e6\u00fe \u00fe\u00e6t n\u00e6fre swa, \u00fe\u00e6t ic wer grete o\u00f0\u00f0e wer me.\n\u00d0a answerden hire \u00fea biscop\u00e6s & hire magas alle, \u00fee on \u00feam temple weron, & cw\u00e6don: God w\u00e6s on\n\u00dea answyrde maria & heom cw\u00e6\u00f0 to: N\u00e6s nan rihtwis men, ne halig \u00e6r abel, & hine arleaslice unwis\nHe brohte twyfealde gyfe drihtene luttre ons\u00e6gednysse & his lichames cl\u00e6nnysse.\nEac swylce helias w\u00e6s of \u00feissere weoruld\u00e6 il\u00e6d on lichame, for\u00fean \u00f0e he his cl\u00e6nnysse heold.\nW\u00e6s heo, swylc heo w\u00e6re feowertene wintr\u00e6.\n\u00dea demden pharisei, \u00fe\u00e6t heo sy\u00f0\u00f0an wuni\u00e6n sceolde on \u00feam godes temple.\n\u00d0\u00e6t \u00feridde d\u00e6g, \u00fea heo \u00fea \u00f0ider isamnod w\u00e6ron, \u00fea astah \u00fee heahbiscop isacar up on \u00feone ytemeste\nGe witon, \u00fe\u00e6t salomon \u00feis temple timbrode & her w\u00e6ron sy\u00f0\u00f0an inne kyning\u00e6 bearn & witegen\u00e6 &\n& heo ilimplice heora yldran w\u00e6ron eawfest\u00e6 & heor\u00e6 bearn \u00e6ft gode icweme lac brohton to \u00feam\nNu is \u00f0onne imetod, \u00fe\u00e6t maria h\u00e6f\u00f0 niwe endebyrdnysse ongunnen gode mid to cwemene, s\u00e6g\u00f0, \u00fe\u00e6t\nUton secan \u00fea andsware \u00e6t gode sylfum ure axunge, \u00fe\u00e6t god us cy\u00fee, hwylce w\u00e6re we hire bif\u00e6sten\n\u00dea licode \u00feet word alle \u00feare samunge and \u00fea senden lot ofer \u00fea tweolf cynn israele bearnum.\n\u00dea feol \u00fe\u00e6t lot ofer iudan cynn, iacobes sune.\n\u00dea bead \u00fee sacerd, \u00fe\u00e6t iudan cynn come \u00fe\u00e6s on m\u00e6rgen to \u00feam godes temple, \u00e6lc \u00fe\u00e6re \u00f0e wif n\u00e6fde,\n\u00dea w\u00e6s \u00f0onen iworden, \u00fe\u00e6t ioseph w\u00e6s ihaten sum iwintred mon & eode \u00feider mid gungum monnum\n\u00dea nam \u00fee sacerd alle gerd\u00e6n & b\u00e6r \u00f0a into Sancta Sanctorum & bead, \u00fe\u00e6t heo comen on m\u00e6rgen &\n\u00deenne scold \u00fee wer beon hyrde \u00feare femn\u00e6n.\n\u00d0a w\u00e6s iworden on m\u00e6rgen \u00fe\u00e6s \u00e6ftren d\u00e6ges, \u00fea comen heo alle on \u00fea tid \u00feare ons\u00e6gednysse, & \u00fea\nW\u00e6s \u00f0are monnum \u00f0reo \u00feusend\u00e6, & \u00fea of nan \u00feare gyrde \u00feeo culfre ut ne eode.\n\u00dea gescrydde hine abiathar \u00fee biscop mid \u00feam heahsacerd\u00e6 gyrlan & in eode on \u00fea Sancta Sanctorum\n\u00dea \u00e6teow him drihtines engel & him to cw\u00e6\u00f0: \u00f0eo s\u00e6leste gerde is git \u00e6fter, \u00fee \u00f0u for noht ne tellest.\nNym \u00fea & syle, \u00feonne cym\u00f0 \u00fe\u00e6t tacn of hire, \u00fe\u00e6t \u00f0u \u00feer secgst.\nW\u00e6s \u00fe\u00e6t iosepes gyrd.\n\u00dea n\u00e6s heo na isoht, for\u00fean \u00f0e ioseph w\u00e6s eald & on utemeste stod.\n\u00dea clypode \u00fee biscop hine mycle stefne & hine nemnode & him his gyrd\u00e6 sealde.\n& \u00fea on s\u00e6mning\u00e6 fleah \u00fe\u00e6r culfre ut swi\u00f0e hwit & fleah geond \u00fea hw\u00e6mmes \u00fe\u00e6s temples & \u00fea\n\u00dea w\u00e6s \u00f0et folc swi\u00f0e gefeonde & cw\u00e6don to iosepe: Eadig eart \u00feu on \u00feine ylde, nu \u00f0e god swa\nEac swylce \u00fea biscop\u00e6